 "note": [
  "Scripture authority is the Open Word Bible (OWB), Balanced edition, Amharic (CC0), bundled offline as backend/library/data/bible/owb-am-b.json.gz and read with translation.fetch_verse_text(\"owb-am\", ref). Every quotation was re-quoted to it verbatim (founder decision, 2026-11-18): a whole verse as the whole OWB verse, a range as its verses joined with a space, a partial quotation as the shortest contiguous OWB span that carries the clause. This replaces the 1962 Amharic Bible (UBS) wording and the translator-rendered Old Testament the first translation used.",
  "A `mined` row is a quotation spliced from OWB by script and checked as an exact substring of the OWB text at its block. Where the author argues from a word the 1962 text used and OWB does not (the rudder, the tongue, gentleness, \"unwholesome\", \"worthless\", the Philippians 4:8 list), the surrounding translated prose was adjusted minimally to OWB's word. `self_rendered` rows are allusions, paraphrases and prayers in the author's own voice, which are prose and were left as translated. Acts 20:35 drops OWB's trailing » (it closes Paul's whole speech, not the verse) so the file's own quote mark closes the quotation."
 ],
